} "Sam Riley"] " (AUS), who won the bronze medal. Riley would return in Atlanta and repeat her bronze medal in this event. Rudovskaya would compete for one more year, this time representing her native Belarus at the 1993 Europeans, where she won a bronze in this event."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "189"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45559"} "Alena Rudkouskaya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/EUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/EUN.png"}] "EUN"]] [:td {} "1:08.75 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:08.00 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "624"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51136"} "Anita Nall"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:09.32 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:08.17 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "34"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45115"} "Sam Riley"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:09.38 (2 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:09.25 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "84"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45767"} "Guylaine Cloutier"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https:/